    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d280">

                <pb facs="0338" n="222" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg222"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1124.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Sullivan.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-02T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 2, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your March 31, 11 p.m. Give what dates in your opinion primary and general
                    elections will be held. Is Constitutional Congress still in session? If so, when
                    will it finish its labors?</p>
                <p>In your utterances you will use caution when speaking of the coming elections and
                    the candidates. The United States has no interest except to aid in the election
                    of the candidate desired by the voters through the medium of free and fair
                    means.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
